body:json {
  {
    "content": "title: React Fundamentals Quest\ndescription: Are you a seasoned JavaScript developer ready to unlock the power of React? This isn't just a quiz; it's your ultimate launchpad! Dive into 'React Fundamentals Quest,' specifically crafted to help you smoothly transition from vanilla JavaScript to the world of declarative UI. Navigate engaging questions that probe essential React concepts – from JSX and components to state management and props – all framed to build upon your existing JS foundation. Solidify your understanding, identify knowledge gaps, and gain the confidence required to tackle your first React projects. Turn your JavaScript expertise into React mastery. Start your quest today!\n\n---question---\ntype: mcq\nquestion: What is JSX primarily used for in React?\ndifficulty: low\noptions:\n1. To write server-side logic\n2. To define database schemas\n3. To describe what the UI should look like [correct]\n4. To manage HTTP requests\ntags: React\n\n---question---\ntype: mcq\nquestion: In a functional React component, how do you update state declared with the `useState` hook?\ndifficulty: medium\noptions:\n1. By directly modifying the state variable\n2. By calling the setter function returned by `useState` [correct]\n3. By using `this.setState()`\n4. By assigning a new value to `props.state`\ntags: React\n\n---question---\ntype: mcq\nquestion: Which of the following best describes React props?\ndifficulty: medium\noptions:\n1. They are mutable data that can be changed by the child component.\n2. They are private data specific to a component that can be changed only by that component.\n3. They are read-only data passed from parent to child components. [correct]\n4. They are functions used to manage side effects in functional components.\ntags: React\n\n---question---\ntype: mcq\nquestion: What does JSX ultimately get transpiled into by Babel?\ndifficulty: medium\noptions:\n1. Pure HTML strings\n2. A single JavaScript object representing the entire DOM\n3. `React.createElement()` calls [correct]\n4. Browser-specific DOM manipulation methods\ntags: React\n\n---question---\ntype: trueFalse\nquestion: The React Virtual DOM is a lightweight copy of the actual DOM, used to improve rendering performance.\ndifficulty: low\ncorrect: true\ntags: React\n\n---question---\ntype: trueFalse\nquestion: React state should be modified directly, for example, by `this.state.count = 5` in a class component.\ndifficulty: medium\ncorrect: false\ntags: React\n\n---question---\ntype: trueFalse\nquestion: All React components must start their names with an uppercase letter.\ndifficulty: low\ncorrect: true\ntags: React\n\n---question---\ntype: trueFalse\nquestion: You can embed any valid JavaScript expression inside JSX by wrapping it in curly braces `{}`.\ndifficulty: low\ncorrect: true\ntags: React\n\n---question---\ntype: written\nquestion: Explain the primary purpose of JSX in a React application.\ndifficulty: low\ntags: React\n\n---question---\ntype: written\nquestion: What is the main difference between \"props\" and \"state\" in React components?\ndifficulty: medium\ntags: React\n\n---question---\ntype: written\nquestion: Describe how you would conditionally render a component or an element in React based on a boolean variable.\ndifficulty: medium\ntags: React\n\n---question---\ntype: written\nquestion: Why is it important to provide a unique `key` prop when rendering a list of items in React?\ndifficulty: high\ntags: React\n\n---question---\ntype: multiSelect\nquestion: Which of the following are common ways to define a component in React?\ndifficulty: low\noptions:\n1. As a JavaScript class that extends `React.Component` [correct]\n2. As a JavaScript function [correct]\n3. As an HTML `<component>` tag\n4. As a plain JavaScript object\ntags: React\n\n---question---\ntype: multiSelect\nquestion: Which of these are benefits of using the React library for UI development?\ndifficulty: medium\noptions:\n1. Declarative UI development [correct]\n2. Efficient updates via the Virtual DOM [correct]\n3. Enforces strict MVC architecture\n4. Provides built-in backend database functionalities\ntags: React\n\n---question---\ntype: multiSelect\nquestion: Which of the following can be passed as `children` to a React component?\ndifficulty: medium\noptions:\n1. Other React elements [correct]\n2. Strings and numbers [correct]\n3. Arrays of React elements [correct]\n4. Functions\ntags: React\n\n---question---\ntype: multiSelect\nquestion: Which of the following are standard React Hooks introduced with React 16.8?\ndifficulty: medium\noptions:\n1. `useEffect` [correct]\n2. `useState` [correct]\n3. `useReducer` [correct]\n4. `useComponentDidMount`\ntags: React"
  }
}
